  "slug": "scientific-fair-5429",
  "summary": "Time-resolved and snapshot spatial data now allow learning explicit cell-cell interaction terms within inferred cell dynamics, including nonreciprocal couplings.",
  "synthesis": "The common thread is inferring dynamical laws governing cell behavior from single-cell and spatial transcriptomics, with interaction terms represented explicitly rather than as descriptive context. A many-body stochastic framework learns cell-cell interaction laws, including nonreciprocal couplings, from experimental multicellular migration trajectories. stMIND applies a continuous-time neural SDE to infer multiscale spatial-temporal interaction dynamics from unmatched time-resolved spatial transcriptomics. CellVocal integrates spatial RNA velocity with cell-cell communication to attribute cell-state transitions to intrinsic and signalling components. SpOTr uses Fused Gromov-Wasserstein optimal transport with a spot deconvolution model to integrate single-cell and spatial transcriptomics data. The Fish Metastasis Atlas addresses a distinct question, organ-specific Ewing sarcoma dissemination in zebrafish, rather than dynamical inference. What is new is the explicit inclusion of signalling and interaction terms within inferred dynamics.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-haiku-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-11-17"
}
